<!-- The setup veil: the full-screen loading overlay shown while the setup
     crate deploys the table (see DeferredSetup.ttslua).

     Every piece is a ROOT element, because an element anchors to its
     parent's edges: nested inside a panel of our own, "top of the screen"
     became the top of that panel instead, and the rule sat well below the
     screen edge. As roots they anchor to the screen, and the ones that
     must span it say so in percent rather than in pixels we cannot know.

     Cotes transposed from Martin's mockup (measured on the 1487x838 canvas
     of his screenshot, scaled by 1920/1487):
       - the band starts 147px from the left edge and is 503px wide
         (26% of the width), full height, black at 65%;
       - the logo is 213x148, centred in the band, its top 94px down;
       - the orange rule is 6px tall, flush with the top edge, spanning the
         screen - it is the progress bar, filling left to right.

     Declared active: the veil has to be up when TTS reveals the table and
     plays its entry camera move, which happens long before Global's onload
     runs. Every path out of the load lowers it, and a timeout lowers it
     even if onload dies halfway.

     setupVeilArt is tinted black rather than hidden: an Image whose
     texture has not downloaded yet renders as a white rectangle, which
     washed the sheet out. Black multiplies it away, and DeferredSetup
     only lifts the tint once the file has actually answered. -->
<Panel
  id="setupVeilGround"
  active="true"
  rectAlignment="MiddleCenter"
  width="12000"
  height="12000"
  color="#05070CFF"
/>

<Image
  id="setupVeilArt"
  active="true"
  rectAlignment="MiddleCenter"
  offsetXY="0 0"
  width="2208"
  height="1242"
  color="#000000FF"
  preserveAspect="true"
/>

